<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
The Developer ID build's entitlements: the release workflow signs the macOS app with them (hardened runtime),
under team G88U5B5783.

- application-identifier, team-identifier, keychain-access-groups: KeychainSecretStore keeps the app's secrets in
  the data protection keychain, which on macOS needs the app's access group. These are restricted entitlements, so the
  app must carry a Developer ID provisioning profile for com.edde746.plezy that grants them
  (Contents/embedded.provisionprofile, from the MACOS_PROVISIONING_PROFILE_BASE64 secret); without one macOS refuses
  to launch the app.
- allow-jit, allow-unsigned-executable-memory: the exceptions for the embedded MPVKit (LuaJIT).
- No App Sandbox, so none of the sandbox's entitlements (network.client, files.user-selected.read-write): outside
  the sandbox the app reaches the network and the files the user picks without them.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.application-identifier</key>
	<string>G88U5B5783.com.edde746.plezy</string>
	<key>com.apple.developer.team-identifier</key>
	<string>G88U5B5783</string>
	<key>keychain-access-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>G88U5B5783.com.edde746.plezy</string>
	</array>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
